Add spoken "press enter" command

Parity with the macOS press-enter feature: saying "…press enter" at the end of
a dictation now strips the trailing command from the pasted text and submits a
Return keystroke so the host app sends.

- Core: PressEnterCommand (pure, regex ported from macOS) detects/strips the
  trailing command; DictationSettings.PressEnterEnabled (default true).
- Core: IKeystrokeSender seam; pipeline pastes the cleaned text then presses
  Enter when detected and enabled.
- Platform: Win32KeystrokeSender (SendInput scan-code Return); wired in DI.
- Tests: L0 PressEnterCommandTests + L3 pipeline tests (enabled/disabled).

Inner loop GREEN at 186.

